  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "My phone is running on Google Pixel 7 Pro. \n\nWhile opening VRChat mobile and clicking launch. Switching my phone to landscape mode. The app crashes each time. Took me a couple weeks to figure it out on what's been going on. I uninstalled it and reinstalled to see if it fixes the issue but has not resolved my issue. \n\nI went the extra step on formatting my phone to see if that resolves my issue. I installing VR Chat mobile again. The app worked as normal. I progressed on setting up my phone again to my original settings . Later on that day I relaunched VRChat again. It crashes once again in landscape mode.\n\nIt got me thinking and upon tinkering with the phone settings. \n\nI went to\n\n-Settings\n\n-Display\n\n-Display size and text\n\nUnder\n\n-Display size\n\nI found out having it on the lowest display size, crashes your VRChat mobile on landscape mode. I had to go up one settings size and relaunched my VRChat and landscape mode was working again! Each time I want to play VRChat mobile. I have to make sure it's set higher than 0 display size to play. I'm happy I found a workaround and able to play VRChat mobile again. \n\nI hope this is useful for someone out there who is experiencing issues as I am.",
